The invariant direct-photon multiplicity as a function of the transverse momentum (\(P_{t}\)) in central Pb+Pb interactions at 17.2 GeV. The figure is taken from [11]. The errors bars indicate the combined statistical and systematic uncertainties. The data points with downward arrows indicate unbounded 90% CL limits on the direct photon yield. The WA98 data points are compared with scaled p+p, p+C results, pQCD calculation and scaled parametrization of direct-photon yields in p+p collisions.
